.el .ds Aq '
.TH shiftpaper-bake 1  shiftpaper 
.SH NAME
shiftpaper\-bake \- Bake a source image into a color + 16\-bit depth PNG pair
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshiftpaper bake\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bake a source image into a color + 16\-bit depth PNG pair.
.PP
Runs the depth model on the source image and writes a pair of files (`<hash>.color.png` and `<hash>.depth16.png`) to the cache directory or the directory specified by \-\-out, printing their paths. Baking the same image again reuses the existing pair. `set` and `slideshow` bake for you, so this is only needed to bake without changing the wallpaper.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output directory. Defaults to the shiftpaper cache directory at $XDG_CACHE_HOME/shiftpaper/wallpapers
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
Path to the ONNX depth model. Falls back to $SHIFTPAPER_MODEL, then [inference] model_path in config.toml
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Source image (jpeg, png, or webp)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
shiftpaper bake photo.jpg                 Bake into the cache
shiftpaper bake photo.jpg \-\-out ~/walls   Bake into a folder of your own
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
shiftpaper(1)
.PP
The docs: https://github.com/CPritch/shiftpaper/tree/main/docs
